<vertex eid="3"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered No" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">R01 [NO]
Matching H01 voltage recordings exist?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">R01 | Matching H01 voltage recordings exist?

Status: NO

Method: Reference boundary

Scope / coordinates: Imported H01 anatomical cells versus the human donor recordings used to constrain their electrical profiles.

Remaining search space: Direct validation against these H01 cells, or prediction constrained by recordings from different human cells.

Binary predicate: A voltage recording is matched by provenance to each imported H01 cell being claimed as directly validated.

Decision limit: Exact cell identity and recording provenance; no substitution of donor identity.

Recorded observation: H01 supplies anatomy and annotations, not voltage recordings matched to the imported cells.

YES: Direct H01-response comparison is available.

NO: Use donor-response validation and label H01 transfer a prediction.

Next check: Retain donor and H01 identities separately in every response record; do not invent an H01 voltage target.

Unresolved after either answer: Neither anatomical identity nor a successful donor fit establishes population-wide human accuracy.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/specs/2026-09-05-h01-recorded-response-acceptance-proposal.md
docs/h01-causal-model.md

