<vertex eid="9"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Open" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000004"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">R03 [OPEN]
Is this response row resolvable?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">R03 | Is this response row resolvable?

Status: OPEN

Method: Hierarchical / measurement

Scope / coordinates: Each event/input/phase separately, at the same frozen candidate, mesh and input conventions.

Remaining search space: Rows with uncertainty below the applicable decision requirement versus rows whose uncertainty prevents that decision.

Binary predicate: Measurement and numerical evidence resolve the proposed comparison under its registered limit.

Decision limit: Use the actual registered per-row limit; usable-tier human spread must be below half its tolerance. Never borrow a limit from another row or window.

Recorded observation: No global resolution verdict is justified: T03/T04 have different timestep outcomes, and interrupted circuit arms have no halving pair.

YES: Interpret the residual and select the appropriate behavior subtree.

NO: Park this row as unresolvable; improve its measurement or numerics first.

Next check: Read retained repeat/refinement evidence for the selected row; state the missing measurement if absent.

Unresolved after either answer: A resolvable row can still fail the contract; an unresolved row cannot pass by a small pooled score.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/specs/2026-09-07-h01-usable-circuit-plan.md
docs/evidence/h01-i-transfer/sp2-close-decision.json
docs/evidence/h01-ie-inhibition/decision.json

